WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.275
When a multiplier has two digits, does the tens digit count as ones?

00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:08.248
Today we are multiplying by two-digit numbers.

00:00:08.468 --> 00:00:14.902
We will separate tens and ones, calculate two partial products, and connect them to the complete multiplication.

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:20.264
Our learning goal is to multiply by two-digit numbers using tens and ones.

00:00:20.914 --> 00:00:22.673
Success criteria.

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:25.964
I can split a multiplier into tens and ones.

00:00:26.184 --> 00:00:29.360
I can label and calculate both partial products.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.379
I can add the products and check their size.

00:00:33.029 --> 00:00:35.455
Thirteen means ten plus three.

00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:40.170
Multiplying by thirteen means taking ten groups and three more groups.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:45.488
Missing the tens value is a common error; label each partial product before adding.

00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:49.649
In a small picture, imagine two rows of thirteen counters.

00:00:49.869 --> 00:00:52.240
Each row has ten and three more.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.015
Both parts still belong in the answer.

00:00:55.665 --> 00:00:59.038
Calculate two hundred and forty-six times thirteen.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:05.099
First take ten groups: two hundred and forty-six times ten is two thousand four hundred and sixty.

00:01:05.749 --> 00:01:11.190
Then take three groups: two hundred and forty-six times three is seven hundred and thirty-eight.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.677
Add the partial products to get three thousand one hundred and ninety-eight.

00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:20.018
Now calculate three hundred and fifteen times twenty-four.

00:01:20.238 --> 00:01:22.537
Twenty-four is twenty plus four.

00:01:22.757 --> 00:01:26.948
Three hundred and fifteen times twenty is six thousand three hundred.

00:01:27.598 --> 00:01:30.807
Four groups make one thousand two hundred and sixty.

00:01:31.027 --> 00:01:36.038
Combining twenty groups and four groups gives seven thousand five hundred and sixty.

00:01:36.688 --> 00:01:39.769
The two in twenty-four means twenty, not two.

00:01:39.989 --> 00:01:43.870
Multiplying by two instead of twenty misses a place value.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.955
Label twenty groups and four groups, then combine the correct partial products.

00:01:49.605 --> 00:01:52.312
What is one hundred and two times twelve?

00:01:56.312 --> 00:02:01.035
Ten groups make one thousand and twenty, and two groups make two hundred and four.

00:02:01.255 --> 00:02:04.472
The total is one thousand two hundred and twenty-four.

00:02:05.122 --> 00:02:08.196
Split the multiplier into tens and ones.

00:02:08.416 --> 00:02:15.620
Calculate both partial products with their correct place values, add them, then check with a nearby friendly multiplication.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.143
Choose a model and explain why your strategy works.
